  "items": [
    {
      "external_id": "C11-PHY-CH2-2.2-DETERMINATION-OF-A-VECTOR-FROM-ITS-RECTANGULAR-COMPONENTS",
      "chapter": "pk-punjab/xi/physics/c11-phy/ch2",
      "topic": "pk-punjab/xi/physics/c11-phy/ch2/u-determination-of-a-vector-from-its-rectangular-components",
      "title": "Determination of a Vector from its Rectangular Components",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "e2c5c034-041b-5340-9823-5e3c8c88a07c",
          "pdf_from": 23,
          "pdf_to": 25,
          "note": "Determination of a Vector from its Rectangular Components: a main subheading of 2.2 Vectors, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 23-25."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "If the rectangular components of a vector as shown in Fig.(2.1) are given, we can find out the magnitude of the vector by using Pythagorean Theorem."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "In the right angle ΔOMP"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "(OP)^2 = (OM)^2 + (MP)^2",
            "text_alt": "(OP)² = (OM)² + (MP)²"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{or}\\quad A^2 = A_x^2 + A_y^2 \\tag{2.4}",
            "text_alt": "or A² = Ax² + Ay²   (2.4)"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{or}\\quad A = \\sqrt{A_x^2 + A_y^2}",
            "text_alt": "or A = √(Ax² + Ay²)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The direction θ is given by"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\tan\\theta = \\frac{MP}{OM} = \\frac{A_y}{A_x}",
            "text_alt": "tan θ = MP/OM = Ay/Ax"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{or}\\quad \\theta = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{A_y}{A_x}\\right) \\tag{2.5}",
            "text_alt": "or θ = tan⁻¹(Ay/Ax)   (2.5)"
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 4,
            "text": "Example 2.1"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Find the angle between two forces of equal magnitude when the magnitude of their resultant is also equal to the magnitude of either of these forces."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Solution: Let θ be the angle between two forces F₁ and F₂, where F₁ is along x-axis. Then",
            "bold": [
              "Solution:"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "x-component of their resultant will be:"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Rx = F₁ cos 0° + F₂ cos θ"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Rx = F₁ + F₂ cos θ"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "And y-component of their resultant is"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Ry = F₁ sin 0° + F₂ sin θ"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Ry = F₂ sin θ"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The resultant R is given by R² = Rx² + Ry²"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "As R = F₁ = F₂ = F"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Hence F² = (F + F cos θ)² + (F sin θ)²"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "F² = F² + F²cos²θ + 2F² cos θ + F² sin²θ"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Or 0 = 2F² cos θ + F² (cos²θ + sin²θ)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "or 0 = 2F² cos θ + F²"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "or cos θ = -0.5"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "or θ = cos⁻¹(-0.5) = 120°"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
